From 38295996604db2491f6480962fb4e422b8496e87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vanetiaho <vangs.vanetia@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:07:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] In-page Spotify playback, aviation-themed GitHub activity,
 polish pass

- Vinyl now plays the featured Spotify track/playlist directly in-page
  via Spotify's iFrame Playback API (real play/pause control, spin
  state driven by actual playback events), instead of just linking out.
  Falls back to the plain embed iframe, then to an external link, if
  the API script can't load. Spotify is now a secondary "Open in
  Spotify" link, not the primary interaction.
- Removed the underline under the hero name; smoothed the easing on
  the letter-bounce and full-width plane-flyover hover animation.
- Fixed the Hero -> About transition: the sunset gradient now hands
  off into a matching horizon-glow wash at the top of About instead of
  cutting to black at the section boundary.
- Replaced the GitHub contribution grid with a custom aviation-themed
  flight path: a plane continuously flies a route whose waypoints
  (one per week) glow brighter with more activity, on a dark panel
  instead of the old beige image fallback. Dropped the image-fallback
  tier entirely (it was the source of the beige background) in favor
  of a clean link-out on failure; kept the retry + response-validation
  reliability logic.
- Added slow-drifting, scroll-parallaxed cloud haze layers to the
  site-wide ambient background for more atmosphere, alongside the
  existing glow blobs and grain.

